<i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ט" data-order="9"></i> The days on which Rosh Chodesh Adar II may properly be fixed: [the mnemonic] &lt;i&gt;zevadlu&lt;/i&gt; [matches weekdays to dates], and [the mnemonic] &lt;i&gt;samech–lamed&lt;/i&gt; for the Sabbaths on which we interrupt [study]: &lt;i&gt;zayin–tes–vav&lt;/i&gt;—when Rosh Chodesh is Shabbos, we interrupt on the fifteenth of that month; the sign is &lt;i&gt;zayin–tes–vav&lt;/i&gt;. When it is Monday, we interrupt on the sixth; sign &lt;i&gt;beis–vav&lt;/i&gt;. When Wednesday, on the fourth; sign &lt;i&gt;daled–daled&lt;/i&gt;. When Friday, on two dates—the second and sixteenth; sign &lt;i&gt;vav beis yud vav&lt;/i&gt;:
